    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0639" n="543" xml:id="pg543"/>

                <head>No. 412.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Biddle.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of. State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 7,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch, No. 61, of the
                    29th of June last, transmitting correspondence with the government of Salvador
                    upon the subject of the neutrality of the interoceanic railway of Honduras, I
                    have to inform you that the position which you have taken in regard to the
                    matter is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
